From: Ross Barnes-Brown <Ross.Barnes-Brown@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: fix NULL srng access during remoteproc recovery

During ath11k firmware crash recovery via remoteproc, the monitor status
ring processing path (ath11k_dp_rx_reap_mon_status_ring) can be invoked
before the srng is fully initialized, resulting in a NULL pointer
dereference in ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin() and a subsequent kernel
panic.

Add an early return guard checking srng->initialized before proceeding
with ring access, preventing the panic during the firmware restart window.

Fixes: kernel panic in ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin during remoteproc recovery
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -3045,6 +3045,9 @@
 
 	srng = &ab->hal.srng_list[rx_ring->refill_buf_ring.ring_id];
 
+	if (!srng->initialized)
+		return 0;
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&srng->lock);
 
 	ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin(ab, srng);
